{"id": 15307, "stem": "<div class=\"relative w-full min-w-0 max-w-full self-stretch\" id=\"question-text\"><span><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><mark class=\"bg-transparent dark:text-neutral-100\" data-markjs=\"true\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">A</mark> 62-year-old man comes to the office due to worsening fatigue.\u00a0 The patient has long-standing type 2 diabetes mellitus complicated by nephropathy.\u00a0 Laboratory results are as follows:</p><div class=\"group/triggerable\" data-is-open=\"false\"><div class=\"group/draggable\" data-is-draggable=\"true\" data-is-dragging=\"false\"><div class=\"group/resizable relative\" data-is-maximized=\"false\" data-is-resizable=\"true\" data-is-resizing=\"false\"><div class=\"relative max-w-full\"><div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"pointer-events-none absolute left-0 top-0 bottom-0 w-8 z-10 transition-opacity duration-200 bg-gradient-to-r from-white dark:from-nbme-primary-dark-800 warm:from-egg-sour-50 to-transparent opacity-0\"></div><div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"pointer-events-none absolute right-0 top-0 bottom-0 w-8 z-10 transition-opacity duration-200 bg-gradient-to-l from-white dark:from-nbme-primary-dark-800 warm:from-egg-sour-50 to-transparent opacity-0\"></div><div class=\"max-w-full overflow-x-auto [&amp;_td]:min-w-[8rem] [&amp;_th]:min-w-[8rem]\"><table class=\"border bg-transparent dark:text-white border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white hover:bg-transparent warm:hover:bg-transparent dark:hover:bg-transparent cursor-default mt-2 mb-3\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><tbody style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; font-size: 1rem;\">Hemoglobin</td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; font-size: 1rem;\">9.4 g/dL</td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; font-size: 1rem;\"></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; font-size: 1rem;\">Mean corpuscular volume</td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; font-size: 1rem;\">90 \u00b5m<sup style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">3</sup></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; font-size: 1rem;\"></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; font-size: 1rem;\">Platelets</td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; font-size: 1rem;\">200,000/mm<sup style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">3</sup></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; font-size: 1rem;\"></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; font-size: 1rem;\">Leukocytes</td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; font-size: 1rem;\">7,500/mm<sup style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">3</sup></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; font-size: 1rem;\"></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; font-size: 1rem;\">Serum creatinine</td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; font-size: 1rem;\">3.2 mg/dL</td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; font-size: 1rem;\"></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; font-size: 1rem;\">Total bilirubin</td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; font-size: 1rem;\">0.8 mg/dL</td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; font-size: 1rem;\"></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; font-size: 1rem;\">Serum ferritin</td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; font-size: 1rem;\">350 ng/mL</td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; font-size: 1rem;\"></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; font-size: 1rem;\">Transferrin saturation</td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; font-size: 1rem;\">35% (normal: 20%-50%)</td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"vertical-align: middle; font-size: 1rem;\"></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">After appropriate treatment is initiated for his anemia, which of the following changes is most likely to occur in this patient's erythroid cells?\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b</p></span></div>", "options": [{"label": "A", "text": "Decrease in mitochondrial iron accumulation"}, {"label": "B", "text": "Decrease in reticuloendothelial destruction"}, {"label": "C", "text": "Increase in progenitor cell differentiation"}, {"label": "D", "text": "Switch of hemoglobin to the fetal form"}, {"label": "E", "text": "Synchronization of nuclear and cytoplasmic maturation"}], "correctAnswer": "C", "explanation": "<div class=\"relative w-full min-w-0 max-w-full self-stretch\" id=\"question-explanation\"><span class=\"\"><div class=\"mb-4 text-start flex justify-start items-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><div class=\"group/triggerable\" data-is-open=\"false\"><div class=\"group/draggable\" data-is-draggable=\"true\" data-is-dragging=\"false\"><div class=\"group/resizable relative\" data-is-maximized=\"false\" data-is-resizable=\"true\" data-is-resizing=\"false\"><div class=\"w-full\"><button class=\"lg:max-w-lg md:max-w-md w-fit max-w-full my-5 hover:scale-[1.01] transition-[transform,_box-shadow] ease-in-out duration-500 hover:shadow-lg\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-none\" src=\"../../Assets/images/b9ro20iyaoxsuc6trl4gxlg3.jpg\"/></button></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><mark class=\"bg-transparent dark:text-neutral-50\" data-markjs=\"true\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">P</mark>atients with <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">chronic kidney disease</strong> (CKD) often develop <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">normocytic anemia</strong> as the glomerular filtration rate declines, primarily due to <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">inadequate production of erythropoietin</strong> (EPO), a hormone secreted by peritubular fibroblasts in the renal cortex.\u00a0 EPO is produced in response to renal hypoxia and acts on erythroid progenitor cells in the bone marrow to reduce apoptosis and increase <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">differentiation</strong> into red blood cells.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Although healthy individuals respond to anemia by markedly increasing EPO production, patients with CKD lose functional EPO-producing cells as renal fibrosis progresses and cannot produce enough EPO to sustain erythropoiesis.\u00a0 This patient's <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">mildly elevated ferritin</strong> reflects chronic inflammation in CKD (ferritin is an acute-phase reactant) and reduced erythropoiesis from EPO deficiency, which lowers iron use and leaves more iron in storage.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Patients with CKD are often treated with <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">recombinant EPO</strong> or its analogs (eg, epoetin, darbepoetin) to stimulate erythropoiesis.\u00a0 Because accelerated red blood cell production rapidly consumes iron, iron stores should be assessed (and repleted if deficient) before treatment.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice A)</strong>\u00a0 Sideroblastic anemia results from inherited or acquired (eg, alcohol use, vitamin B6 deficiency, lead poisoning) defects in heme synthesis.\u00a0 Iron that cannot be incorporated into heme accumulates in erythroid mitochondria (ringed sideroblasts), and treating the underlying cause reduces this accumulation.\u00a0 However, sideroblastic anemia causes iron overload with elevated transferrin saturation, which this patient does not have.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice B)</strong>\u00a0 Warm <a class=\"hint\" data-exhibit-id=\"exhibit-febisiivnlyqrziw4pbpe4yn\" href=\"#exhibit-exhibit-febisiivnlyqrziw4pbpe4yn\">autoimmune hemolytic anemia</a> is caused by IgG antibodies against red cell membrane antigens, leading to phagocytosis in the reticuloendothelial system (eg, spleen).\u00a0 Autoimmune hemolytic anemia is usually treated with glucocorticoids (eg, prednisone), which reduce macrophage destruction of antibody-coated red cells and decrease autoantibody production.\u00a0 This patient's normal bilirubin makes hemolytic anemia unlikely.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice D)</strong>\u00a0 Sickle cell anemia results from a point mutation in the \u03b2-globin gene that causes deoxygenated hemoglobin to polymerize (\"sickling\").\u00a0 Treatment with hydroxyurea induces expression of fetal hemoglobin (which lacks \u03b2-globin chains), reducing polymerization.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice E)</strong>\u00a0 Vitamin B<sub style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">12</sub>/folate deficiency (megaloblastic anemia) impairs DNA synthesis, so nuclear maturation of erythroid precursors lags behind cytoplasmic maturation.\u00a0 Replacement restores DNA synthesis and synchronizes nuclear and cytoplasmic maturation.\u00a0 Megaloblastic anemia causes macrocytosis (elevated mean corpuscular volume), whereas this patient's anemia is normocytic.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Educational objective:</strong>Erythropoietin (EPO) is produced by renal peritubular fibroblasts in response to hypoxia and acts on erythroid progenitor cells in the bone marrow to promote their survival and differentiation into red blood cells.\u00a0 Loss of EPO-producing cells in chronic kidney disease causes normocytic anemia, which is treated with recombinant EPO.\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b</p></span></div>", "educationalObjective": "Erythropoietin (EPO) is produced by renal peritubular fibroblasts in response to hypoxia and acts on erythroid progenitor cells in the bone marrow to promote their survival and differentiation into red blood cells.  Loss of EPO-producing cells in chronic kidney disease causes normocytic anemia, which is treated with recombinant EPO.\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b", "subject": "Physiology", "system": "Hematology & Oncology", "topic": "Erythropoietin", "category": "Red blood cell disorders", "peerCorrect": 44.0}